## Building a Weekly Planner

Each day has an activity. Different activities carry different data: work has hours, exercise has minutes, social has friend count, rest has nothing.

### The Activity Enum

```xiom
enum Activity {
  Work(hours: Int),
  Exercise(minutes: Int),
  Rest,
  Social(friends: Int),
}
```

### The DayPlan Struct

```xiom
type DayPlan = {
  day: Str;
  activity: Activity;
}
```

### Creating a Plan

```xiom
let monday = DayPlan{
  day: "Monday";
  activity: Activity.Work(8);
};

let tuesday = DayPlan{
  day: "Tuesday";
  activity: Activity.Exercise(45);
};

let wednesday = DayPlan{
  day: "Wednesday";
  activity: Activity.Rest;
};
```

### Summarizing a Day

Match on the activity to build a description:

```xiom
fn DayPlan.summary(self) -> Str {
  match activity {
    Work(hours) => { return day + ": Work for " + hours + " hours"; }
    Exercise(minutes) => { return day + ": Exercise for " + minutes + " minutes"; }
    Rest => { return day + ": Rest day"; }
    Social(friends) => { return day + ": Hang out with " + friends + " friends"; }
  }
}
```

### Planning the Week

```xiom
monday.summary();     // "Monday: Work for 8 hours"
tuesday.summary();    // "Tuesday: Exercise for 45 minutes"
wednesday.summary();  // "Wednesday: Rest day"
```

### Computing Totals

```xiom
fn total_work_hours(plan: DayPlan) -> Int {
  match plan.activity {
    Work(hours) => { return hours; }
    _ => { return 0; }
  }
}
```

